00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:59.520
a person comes to you from
one of your sort of line

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:02.820
of business, and
say, I need this app.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:05.980
I'm using, let's say, one of
the ERP app or the CRM app,

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:10.290
but I need this one little thing
or this one little workflow.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.300
And your answer
typically will be,

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:15.730
yeah, I know, I have this
in 100 projects on my plate.

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:16.949
So this goes to the bottom.

00:03:16.949 --> 00:03:18.990
Or the guy might say, hey,
this is the number one

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:24.430
priority for our CXO, so you
need to get going on this fast.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:27.470
So then you have to drop
something from your plate

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:28.860
to take this on, right?

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:33.580
Why does that happens?

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:36.730
That happens
because you cannot--

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:39.740
even with all the solutions that
are available in the market,

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:43.060
you cannot meet all the needs
of all the people that you need

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:46.180
to serve in your organization,
all the time, right?

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:48.910
So there is a gap
in the app space.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:51.940
And you only have the
skill to build that,

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:55.186
and when someone new comes in,
a line of business partner,

00:03:55.186 --> 00:03:56.810
you don't have the
skill to build that.

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:58.300
So that is a skill gap.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.070
So there's two solution to that.

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:04.650
So one is make all your
line-of-business partners

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.370
to acquire the skills
that you have so

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:10.810
that everybody can develop, or
probably a better solution is,

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:14.160
make the platform such
that anybody can develop.

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:17.230
Make the non-developers,
or the people

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:20.019
who are in the line of
business, developers.

00:04:20.019 --> 00:04:22.790
Give them the tools so
that they can develop.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.930
If you do that, then they
can build on their own,

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:27.490
so you're bridging
the skill gap,

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.260
and they can build
the app that they

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:31.030
want instead of coming to you.

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:34.330
So that is the app gap,
and the skills gap concept.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.460
If you're successful
in both, then you

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:40.510
will allow application to
be built quickly and easily.

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:43.150
Let me double down on that, and
break this mission into-- sort

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:45.400
of into three things which
are a little more concrete.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:51.500
When you use G Suite,
you know, you have--

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.644
like from a database, you want
to bring it out to Sheets.

00:04:54.644 --> 00:04:56.810
You need to have approval
workflow with the identity

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:59.860
that you have many of
these applications.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:02.910
So all this may not
be easily provided

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:05.500
in the off-the-shelf
solution that we provide.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:09.530
So that means you have
to extend G Suite to meet

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:12.100
these functionality needs.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:17.850
And as I talked about, we
want to enable that use case

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.550
for both developers
and non-developers,

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:26.190
so that is our first goal, to
make it useful to everyone.

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:30.960
And the second thing is we want
to offer this as a platform.

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:34.140
Today, many of the tools
that you might be using,

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:38.490
things like App Maker, or
Apps Script, and other tools,

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:41.179
they are offered sort
of as disparate products

00:05:41.179 --> 00:05:41.720
on their own.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:42.990
They stand on their own.

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:46.000
But what we want to do is
bring to you a platform,

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.780
which provides the end-to-end
experience for a developer,

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:51.420
so that whatever you
need as a developer--

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:54.090
and here, you know, I'm talking
about non-developers also--

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:56.950
it is provided that.

00:05:56.950 --> 00:05:58.970
So that is the first thing.

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:01.150
The second thing is
that I want to hit on

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:04.600
is the concept of assistive
experience and enterprise

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:06.900
knowledge.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:10.050
So let me explain
what I mean by that.

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:13.695
So let's talk about
enterprise knowledge first.

00:06:13.695 --> 00:06:17.490
So let's say, you know,
you join a company new.

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:22.030
And you are tasked with
doing contract negotiations.

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:24.210
You don't know how
contract negotiations

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:25.960
happen in your company.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:26.740
So what do you do?

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:29.760
The first thing you do is
talk to your supervisor,

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:31.890
or talk to your colleagues,
or talk to your friends

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:35.700
in the company, to figure
out who is the person who

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:39.990
has done this before, and how
can I approach that person,

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:42.280
or talk to that person?

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:45.090
So then that person maybe
direct you to some other person,

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:47.700
and then you eventually
reach that person.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:49.500
So that means this
knowledge that is there

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:51.660
in the enterprise,
which is, who is

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:54.960
the expert here in
this particular area,

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:56.470
is not institutionalized.

00:06:56.470 --> 00:07:00.260
It is there in
someone's head, right?

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:03.520
The same thing applies
to things like document.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.430
Which are the best
documents that describe

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:07.197
contract negotiation process?

00:07:07.197 --> 00:07:08.030
You don't know that.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:09.155
You are new to the company.

00:07:09.155 --> 00:07:12.060
And there is no way
you can get that.

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:15.800
And that knowledge is, again,
with someone who knows what

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:18.260
is the document that
you need to refer to.

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:20.160
These are sort of the
enterprise knowledge,

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:21.035
we are talking about.

00:07:21.035 --> 00:07:23.120
And you can extend
this to, let's say,

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:24.410
who are our best customers?

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:27.410
Who are our most loyal customers
that we want to take care of?

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:29.840
Who are best customer
service representatives?

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:32.490
These are knowledge that
is there in the enterprise.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:35.550
And it is not in an
accessible format

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:37.680
or not in
institutionalized format.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:40.300
So that's what the enterprise
knowledge refers to.

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:44.360
It is that the knowledge that
is there in the enterprise,

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:46.770
is it there in an
accessible format or not,

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:49.640
or is it in someone's head?

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:51.770
The second concept
here is what we are

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:53.780
calling assistive experience.

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:57.170
Assistive means
something which allows

00:07:57.170 --> 00:07:59.570
you to do your main task.

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:02.390
It helps you to
do your main task.

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:05.620
It doesn't take over the
task, but in some way

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:07.910
it takes away the
mundane from the task,

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:10.400
and help you focus
on the main task.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:12.470
So let me give you a
real world example.

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:16.760
So any of us who is driving
a little bit of a newer car

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:20.050
will know that you have lot
of what is called drive assist

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:22.940
features, so keep
you in the lane,

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:25.010
allow you to look
at the blind spot,

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:28.700
or warn you to look at the
blind spot, adaptive cruise.

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:31.430
The main task, which is
driving, is not going away,

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:35.000
but some of these
side tasks the vehicle

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:39.260
allows you to take care so that
you can just focus on driving.

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:42.230
Now remember this is completely
different from autonomous

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:43.980
driving, which is the
main task, which is

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:45.530
the driving getting replaced.

00:08:45.530 --> 00:08:49.190
So the assistive experience is
taking away some of the task

00:08:49.190 --> 00:08:50.750
and helps you drive.

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:54.090
So let's bring it back
to sort of our world,

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:56.300
and I'll give you three
different examples

00:08:56.300 --> 00:09:01.940
of like in IT how it is useful.

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:04.020
Think about an end
user experience.

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:06.710
So the end user experience--
and you might probably have seen

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:07.990
this in the keynote--

00:09:07.990 --> 00:09:10.940
is all of us, we
schedule meetings.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:13.550
So when you schedule
meetings, we

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:18.740
can say that, OK, I want
to meet person x and y.

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:24.100
Won't it be nice if I exchange
sort of mails with someone,

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:29.020
and from the mail I can just
hit something, hit a button,

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:32.350
and it goes, based on the
context, and schedules

00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:33.870
a meeting?

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:35.660
And it not only
schedules a meeting,

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:37.290
it finds out the
meeting room for you.

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:39.690
So this is truly possible.

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:44.911
What you want next is or
to make it more magical is,

00:09:44.911 --> 00:09:46.910
based on the context,
based on the understanding

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:51.620
of the context, if you
are able to figure out

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:54.110
what are the document that will
be relevant to the context,

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:57.340
and you provide the links
in that meeting invite.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:10:00.490
What will even be more magical--
because a lot of us have

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:02.170
to write an agenda
for the meeting,

00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:05.200
it's based on what I will
discuss and it is happening--

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:09.800
it provides a draft agenda
in the invite itself.

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:12.430
So that is an example
of assistive experience,

00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:14.230
because you still
have do the meeting,

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:16.330
but this part of
scheduling the meeting

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:18.100
and drafting an
agenda and things

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:20.590
like that, you don't
have to do anymore,

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:23.050
so that is taken care
of by the system.

00:10:23.050 --> 00:10:24.640
So that is an
assistive experience

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.440
in an end user sense.

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:27.860
Now think of an admin.

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:29.530
If you're an
enterprise admin, you

00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:31.826
are thinking of buying
different applications

00:10:31.826 --> 00:10:32.700
from the marketplace.

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:36.160
Let's say you go to the
G Suite marketplace,

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:39.310
and you are getting,
or you are trying

00:10:39.310 --> 00:10:41.440
to decide what are
the applications that

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:43.760
would be helpful to me.

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:46.570
So in that context,
let's say, today you

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:48.430
go to the G suite marketplace.

00:10:48.430 --> 00:10:50.620
It just shows you
a lot of apps based

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:52.660
on popularity or some criteria.

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:56.840
It is not contextualized
to your own situation.

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:59.350
So in a world of tomorrow,
what will happen is,

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:03.050
based on whatever is
ongoing in your enterprise,

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:05.434
the marketplace, the
app in the marketplace,

00:11:05.434 --> 00:11:06.850
the automation in
the marketplace,

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:10.690
or the items in the marketplace,
is curated to your need.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:13.810
The system understand
what you need right now

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:18.430
and shows you the
applications or the items

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:20.790
that you need right now.

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:23.750
And that means the admin can
choose the application that he

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:25.630
needs much more easier way.

00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:29.400
Now, let's say it gives you
three different choices.

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:33.070
What will happen is the admin
will go look at the reviews

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:35.410
or figure out how good
the application is

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:38.370
and do some evaluation and
bring it to the enterprise.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:42.980
Won't it be nice if the
reviews are summarized for you,

00:11:42.980 --> 00:11:45.770
and the pros and cons
are spelled out for you,

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:48.890
and based on your need you
can dial up and dial down,

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:53.420
and based on that you decide
which applications to buy?

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:59.080
That is another example of admin
using assistive experience.

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:02.030
And the same thing can we
think about a developer, where

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:04.580
based on what kind of
code you are writing,

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:09.770
if you are writing a code on,
let's say, accessing mail API,

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:12.470
we know the pattern
is, after the mail API,

00:12:12.470 --> 00:12:15.410
you invoke a Calendar API,
we can suggest you the code

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:18.230
blocks, so that you
can build that app.

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:21.780
So that is an assistive
experience for developers.

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:25.370
So we want to enable those
sort of experience which

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:31.520
takes care of assistive, as
well as enterprise knowledge.

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:34.160
The third thing, like I
talked about, our goal here

00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:36.020
is to make this kind
of technologies,

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:37.970
build this capabilities
into the platform,

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:40.220
so that it is
accessible to everyone.

00:12:40.220 --> 00:12:44.000
All kinds of developers, and
all kinds of non-developers,

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:45.920
everybody in the
enterprise should

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:50.590
be able to access these
sort of applications.

00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:52.360
So those are our
three key goals.

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:56.060
Now imagine if we
are successful.

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:57.640
So this goes to the
online developer,

00:12:57.640 --> 00:12:58.660
developer, developer.

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:03.010
You know where this came
from, and we want that.

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:06.840
But developers
are a finicky lot.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:10.120
They don't adapt a platform
unless and until it

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:11.920
is useful for them.

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:15.027
We think by making it
really quick and really easy

00:13:15.027 --> 00:13:16.860
so that you can visually
compose application

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:20.650
all with a little bit of
code and bringing together

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:23.200
this assistive experience
with the ability

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:25.600
to access enterprise
knowledge, we'll

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:29.470
be able to create enough
differences that developers

00:13:29.470 --> 00:13:31.130
will be willing to
adapt this platform.

00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:36.660
Now if they adapt this
platform, what do we get?

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:39.830
We get lots and lots
of intelligent apps.

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:42.470
These are intelligent,
because you

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:44.090
are building
assistive experience

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:46.010
using enterprise knowledge.

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:50.360
And what you can do is you
can combine first party, which

00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:54.230
is Google Cloud and G Suite
apps, with third party, which

00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:56.750
is a different service provider,
and you are in the middle.

00:13:56.750 --> 00:14:00.920
You can orchestrate within
all three different ecosystem

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:04.490
to build the right kind
of apps that you need.

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:07.490
And that itself leads
to a virtuous ecosystem

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:08.510
which creates a lot of--

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:10.520
lots and lots of apps.

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:13.160
Now the key message of
this particular platform

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.020
is knowledge intelligence.

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:18.080
Now let's discuss how
knowledge intelligence is

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:20.880
different from
enterprise knowledge.

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:22.850
Now remember, in an
enterprise knowledge,

00:14:22.850 --> 00:14:28.220
you have to pre-think
what exactly you want.

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:31.640
If you want-- who are
your loyal customers

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:33.830
or who is the best customer
service representative,

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:37.010
you have to think through and
build this into the system

00:14:37.010 --> 00:14:38.990
and make it accessible
to the system,

00:14:38.990 --> 00:14:42.020
accessible to the application
using some particular system

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:44.100
or some particular algorithm.

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:46.820
So that is an explicit
declarative way

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:49.200
of getting this information.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:51.560
Now, like business
intelligence, if we

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:53.900
provide you the capability
by which you can

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:55.880
leverage your own data, right?

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:57.650
You know, you control your data.

00:14:57.650 --> 00:15:00.920
And using the technology
that we provide,

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:03.530
you don't have to
pre-think that beforehand,

00:15:03.530 --> 00:15:07.400
but we will allow
you to take advantage

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:09.950
of the information that is
there in your enterprise

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:12.170
and extract out
those information

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:15.270
and make it accessible
to your application.

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:17.300
So that is what knowledge
intelligence means.

00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:19.550
It is an informed
knowledge versus

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:22.100
an explicit and declarative
knowledge, right?

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:25.640
So imagine, if you are
able to do that, then you

00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:26.570
know what is possible.

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:28.720
Is Google-- when I said,
Google could understand that,

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:31.053
and, of course, you know, we
will build that capability,

00:15:31.053 --> 00:15:32.870
but then it's up
to you whether you

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:34.940
want to take advantage
of this capability to get

00:15:34.940 --> 00:15:36.530
more out of your business.

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:39.290
So if you get able
to do that, if you're

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:43.580
able to leverage this
knowledge intelligence,

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:45.920
along with the
developer platform

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:51.470
which allows you to take
advantage of all the things

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:54.870
that are there, then
imagine what you can build.

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:59.650
So you can build the next
generation of app, the apps

00:15:59.650 --> 00:16:05.330
that we talked about, where you
can potentially have a customer

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:09.290
support call from your
most loyal customer routed

00:16:09.290 --> 00:16:10.970
through the best
representative that

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:15.020
can serve that particular
customer at that instant,

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:18.260
those kind of game changing
apps that you can build,

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:21.360
which can really
transform your business.

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:23.800
So to summarize, what
are we going to do?

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:27.270
So we are going to help you
build these new apps, which

00:16:27.270 --> 00:16:29.310
can rethink your business.

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:32.760
And to do that,
what we will do is

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:35.250
we'll help you
gather information

00:16:35.250 --> 00:16:38.790
about your processes,
people, systems,

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:42.600
and we will derive the
insights and provide

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:46.270
the tools that allow you
to tap into the systems.

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:48.570
And once you tap
into the system,

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:52.300
you can then build sort of the
next generation of productivity

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:55.140
app using some [INAUDIBLE]
and other techniques

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:57.810
to predict and automate
a lot of these tasks.

00:16:57.810 --> 00:17:01.370
So that is what you can do with
this next generation of apps

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:03.970
that you are going to build.

00:17:03.970 --> 00:17:06.430
But the question is,
this is a grand vision.

00:17:06.430 --> 00:17:08.800
Are we-- how we think
we are able to do that?

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:11.500
You know, this is like
nice smoke and mirrors.

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:14.290
What makes us think
that we will be

00:17:14.290 --> 00:17:16.480
able to build that capability?

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:18.400
I think there are two
fundamental arguments.

00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:20.079
There's the Google
way of looking at it,

00:17:20.079 --> 00:17:22.599
and that's what makes
us sort of confident

00:17:22.599 --> 00:17:26.530
that we'll be able
to hit those goals.

00:17:26.530 --> 00:17:31.150
So number one, we are primarily
a cloud native platform, so

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:34.660
that means, anything that
you use-- primal everything,

00:17:34.660 --> 00:17:36.640
the whole corpus
of information--

00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:38.110
resides in the cloud.

00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:40.360
There is no, sort
of, for most part,

00:17:40.360 --> 00:17:43.395
on prem and off prm
kind of a thing.

00:17:43.395 --> 00:17:44.270
What does that allow?

00:17:44.270 --> 00:17:45.310
That allows two things.

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:49.050
One is, because we are at
one place on the cloud,

00:17:49.050 --> 00:17:51.982
so that means the
knowledge itself is not

00:17:51.982 --> 00:17:53.440
split between two
different places,

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:57.030
so that means we have the
full picture of the knowledge.

00:17:57.030 --> 00:18:01.350
The second thing is, the
most real-time information

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:03.120
is available in the cloud.

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:06.330
So, the context, for example,
whether you are at work,

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:08.970
whether you are at home,
whether you are holding

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:11.820
a mobile device, or whether
you are on a desktop,

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:13.780
that information is available.

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:16.020
And that is relevant,
because the way

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:19.720
you deliver the application
will be dependent on that.

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:23.310
So the cloud native way
allows you to, first of all,

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:25.590
get the complete
set of information,

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:29.080
and allow the most
real-time decision possible.

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:31.170
So that is the first advantage.

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:34.690
And the second advantage we have
is in AI and machine learning.

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:37.545
We think that we have
earned the right, based

00:18:37.545 --> 00:18:39.510
on some of the things
that we have done.

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:41.940
We are phenomenally better
than our competition

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:44.940
in understanding the
space and delivering

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:46.880
sort of on applications
that leverage

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:49.680
this sort of technologies.

00:18:49.680 --> 00:18:54.030
And using those tools, I think
we can realize the vision

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:56.000
that we just talked about.

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:57.550
I talked about
developer platform.

00:18:57.550 --> 00:19:00.150
So what does the development
platform is made up of?

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:02.310
So like any other
developer platform,

00:19:02.310 --> 00:19:05.490
we'll provide the best
available developer platform.

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:07.887
We will provide all
these different things

00:19:07.887 --> 00:19:09.720
that you expect out of
a developer platform.

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:11.074
We'll provide tools.

00:19:11.074 --> 00:19:12.240
We'll provide documentation.

00:19:12.240 --> 00:19:13.680
We'll provide Canonical Apps.

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:15.450
We'll provide APIs.

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:17.299
We'll help build the community.

00:19:17.299 --> 00:19:19.590
And competence is one of the
different pieces I'm going

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:21.430
to talk in the following slide.

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:23.970
But essentially, you can
take the platform and use

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:27.750
that to orchestrate between
the first party, which

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:34.020
is the Google services and
applications with third party

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:35.990
using the platform.

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:38.482
And we'll offer this in
an integrated fashion.

00:19:38.482 --> 00:19:40.440
So it will be a unified
experience in the sense

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:41.970
that it'll look
like it is coming

00:19:41.970 --> 00:19:46.880
from the same company
or the same provider

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:49.440
instead of looking
very disparate.

00:19:49.440 --> 00:19:53.849
And this will be consisting of
this particular aspect, which

00:19:53.849 --> 00:19:55.140
is the development environment.

00:19:55.140 --> 00:19:58.250
We'll provide you the
coordinating tool,

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:00.240
and the components, and tools.

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:01.800
We'll provide the runtime.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:04.140
We'll provide different
infrastructure tools,

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:07.290
and these will be infrastructure
in terms of administering

00:20:07.290 --> 00:20:09.120
your app, monitoring your app.

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:11.490
And we'll provide a
marketplace in which

00:20:11.490 --> 00:20:13.620
you can publish these apps.

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:15.360
And we'll help
you take advantage

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:19.870
of, as I said, in a G Suite
ecosystem, the GCP ecosystem,

00:20:19.870 --> 00:20:21.480
and the third party services.

00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:27.550
All these three will be
critical for your success.

00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:29.620
So now let's talk about
something concrete.

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:31.560
What are the pieces or
what are the components

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:33.340
of this platform?

00:20:33.340 --> 00:20:37.790
So like I said, all
these tools will

00:20:37.790 --> 00:20:40.230
be integrated into one
platform-- the developer

00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:41.890
platform.

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:44.490
So the first column
that we talked about

00:20:44.490 --> 00:20:49.090
is the different development
tools and the runtime.

00:20:49.090 --> 00:20:52.560
So we have an App Maker, Apps
Script, and add-ons there.

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:57.270
Our goal is to make App Maker
sort of the no-code solution

00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:58.690
to build your app.

00:20:58.690 --> 00:20:59.910
So it may not be there.

00:20:59.910 --> 00:21:03.900
It may fall short right now
in realizing the vision,

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:07.710
but the goal there is we should
provide a visually composable

00:21:07.710 --> 00:21:11.460
way to build an app, and
that's why App Maker is there,

00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:13.290
and that is the no-code segment.

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:16.940
And Apps Script
will be what we call

00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:19.610
the low-code segment,
where with some code

00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:21.200
you'll be able to build that.

00:21:21.200 --> 00:21:25.710
And add-ons is about bringing
together the host application

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:29.250
context into your application
that you are building.

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:31.980
So that is the first thing
that we are going to offer.

00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:34.880
The second thing is
once you build the app,

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:39.860
you need a way to publish it so
that other people can use that.

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:42.140
It could be in your
domain, or it could

00:21:42.140 --> 00:21:44.090
be outside of your domain.

00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:48.410
And we will make sure that the
published part of it from each

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:53.540
of this development environment,
you can easily publish that,

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:56.420
and the admin can easily bring
into their enterprise using

00:21:56.420 --> 00:21:58.770
the marketplace.

00:21:58.770 --> 00:22:02.350
The third column there is
data connectors, automation,

00:22:02.350 --> 00:22:04.070
and APIs.

00:22:04.070 --> 00:22:08.590
Now we acknowledge that today we
don't have a good story there.

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:10.980
That is a gap that
we acknowledge,

00:22:10.980 --> 00:22:13.920
and we are working to fix that.

00:22:13.920 --> 00:22:18.850
Data connectors will be sort
of a connection mechanism

00:22:18.850 --> 00:22:21.790
to your on prem
and other clouds.

00:22:21.790 --> 00:22:27.820
And we understand that, today,
there is no way from G Suite

00:22:27.820 --> 00:22:29.440
to do that.

00:22:29.440 --> 00:22:32.620
We are thinking about
it and working on it,

00:22:32.620 --> 00:22:37.980
and you should hear
more in probably--

00:22:37.980 --> 00:22:40.980
soon, next few months, you
should be hearing something

00:22:40.980 --> 00:22:41.970
about that.

00:22:41.970 --> 00:22:43.920
So this will allow
you to access--

00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:47.010
because you know, right now,
we know all of us cannot move

00:22:47.010 --> 00:22:50.850
to cloud straightaway, so we'll
have some on prm some off prm

00:22:50.850 --> 00:22:54.755
So it is important that we
connect the on prm off prm

00:22:54.755 --> 00:22:56.880
experience, and the data
connectors will be the way

00:22:56.880 --> 00:22:58.640
to do that.

00:22:58.640 --> 00:23:01.180
The second thing is on
automation and workflow.

00:23:01.180 --> 00:23:03.220
In the enterprise
workload, you may

00:23:03.220 --> 00:23:07.210
have lot of interprocess flows
which needs to be automated,

00:23:07.210 --> 00:23:10.540
and both from a
line-of-business standpoint,

00:23:10.540 --> 00:23:13.720
and from individual standpoint,
individual productivity

00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:14.800
standpoint.

00:23:14.800 --> 00:23:19.090
And today, we don't have
a clear solution there.

00:23:19.090 --> 00:23:22.480
Again, this is one of the
space that we are working on,

00:23:22.480 --> 00:23:27.660
and this will allow you to build
automations in a no-code way,

00:23:27.660 --> 00:23:31.430
and that's what we are
looking forward to.

00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:35.830
And we hope we will
have something for you

00:23:35.830 --> 00:23:39.560
in the next few months.

00:23:39.560 --> 00:23:42.820
And the third thing is APIs.

00:23:42.820 --> 00:23:45.830
Traditionally, our API surface
has not been very smooth,

00:23:45.830 --> 00:23:48.540
and if you have
developed using our API,

00:23:48.540 --> 00:23:52.250
you will see it has been a
little bit rough on the edges.

00:23:52.250 --> 00:23:53.450
We are looking at that.

00:23:53.450 --> 00:23:57.230
We will make sure that we take
a API first approach where

00:23:57.230 --> 00:23:59.900
all our products
have APIs, and they

00:23:59.900 --> 00:24:02.550
are accessible in the same way.

00:24:02.550 --> 00:24:06.290
And so stay tuned, and
we will have more things

00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:10.590
to talk about in the next
few quarters or few months.

00:24:10.590 --> 00:24:12.730
And the last part of it
is administrative tools.

00:24:12.730 --> 00:24:17.450
We acknowledge that we are not--
we don't have a great story.

00:24:17.450 --> 00:24:19.580
We have been delivering
features on that,

00:24:19.580 --> 00:24:22.670
but it is not an integrated
suite of admin tools

00:24:22.670 --> 00:24:24.680
that we have
delivered, but again

00:24:24.680 --> 00:24:27.620
that is something which
we understand and we

00:24:27.620 --> 00:24:28.820
will be delivering that.

00:24:28.820 --> 00:24:32.660
So all those four pieces will
form the backbone of developer

00:24:32.660 --> 00:24:37.650
platforms, and that is what we
want to deliver going forward.

00:24:37.650 --> 00:24:39.770
So, on that journey,
you know, this

00:24:39.770 --> 00:24:42.310
is the first thing we would
like to announce today, right.

00:24:42.310 --> 00:24:45.380
In all our projects,
all our tools, now we

00:24:45.380 --> 00:24:48.950
will have one single place
where you can access.

00:24:48.950 --> 00:24:51.680
So, whether it is API,
documentations, community,

00:24:51.680 --> 00:24:54.740
or anything like
that, all the tools.

00:24:54.740 --> 00:24:57.680
We are calling it the
G Suite Developer Hub,

00:24:57.680 --> 00:25:02.330
and now instead of
going to different URLs,

00:25:02.330 --> 00:25:05.180
you just go to this place,
and you'll get everything

00:25:05.180 --> 00:25:07.550
that you need from this place.

00:25:07.550 --> 00:25:11.420
And we are in the process
of rolling this out.

00:25:11.420 --> 00:25:13.845
We will provide
you the exact URL.

00:25:13.845 --> 00:25:19.250
This will get plugged in to
the G Suite developer site,

00:25:19.250 --> 00:25:21.110
or the Google developer site.

00:25:21.110 --> 00:25:24.470
And this is all you need
to know going forward.

00:25:24.470 --> 00:25:26.850
All our new product,
new features,

00:25:26.850 --> 00:25:29.960
new documentation, everything
will come into this place.

00:25:29.960 --> 00:25:32.650
OK?

00:25:32.650 --> 00:25:36.310
The second part of our
journey is App Maker.

00:25:36.310 --> 00:25:38.200
So thank you for people
who have been using

00:25:38.200 --> 00:25:39.470
App Maker for a long time.

00:25:39.470 --> 00:25:41.320
It took a long time to GA.

00:25:41.320 --> 00:25:44.590
But I think you know we have
App Maker in a good place right

00:25:44.590 --> 00:25:45.370
now.

00:25:45.370 --> 00:25:48.790
We launched on 14 June, so
it's been about a month,

00:25:48.790 --> 00:25:51.377
but the response
from the enterprises

00:25:51.377 --> 00:25:52.210
has been tremendous.

00:25:52.210 --> 00:25:55.010
So these are the number
of customers to domains

00:25:55.010 --> 00:25:57.250
here matched to customers.

00:25:57.250 --> 00:26:01.630
And we have more than 3,000
apps that have been developed.

00:26:01.630 --> 00:26:03.700
